 - **Integrity (M06-M08, M17):** the full hard-fail vector (glass, h1, placeholders, centred, type sizes, hero gradient, purple-blue, icon rows, accent, spacing off-scale, overflow, clipped, offscreen-left, unreachable, scrolled text, unmeasured, reflow, contrast) is compared page world vs probe world and with JavaScript off, on the positional page and on every declared state. Contrast is a custom diagnostic (text vs resolved solid background, 4.5:1 / 3:1), not axe: axe cannot run with JavaScript off. JavaScript-off content (visible copy slots, h1 count, lang, dir) must match or the cross-check is INCOMPLETE. UNTESTED: text over images or gradients in the contrast diagnostic (counted as unknown, not failed); the native-function check stays a heuristic.
-- **320 px reflow (M01, M02, M09-M11, M14):** scrollers are measured with their own text, open shadow roots and same-origin frames; content outside a scroller's reachable range is `unreachable` at every width; keyboard use means an explicit `tabindex >= 0` scroller or usable targets that step across the whole extent; candidates and their exceptions are scoped to screen/state/lang. UNTESTED: closed shadow roots, `overflow: overlay`, scroll snapping, and whether a resolved candidate genuinely needs 2D layout (the reviewer's decision).
+- **320 px reflow (M01, M02, M09-M11, M14):** scrollers are measured with their own text, open shadow roots and same-origin frames; content outside a scroller's reachable range is `unreachable` at every width; keyboard use means an explicit `tabindex >= 0` scroller or usable targets that step across the whole extent; candidates and their exceptions are scoped to screen/state/lang. UNTESTED: closed shadow roots, `overflow: overlay`, scroll snapping, and whether a resolved candidate genuinely needs 2D layout (the reviewer's decision). *(Superseded in part by R13 N21: same-origin frames are partially inspected and fail the handoff anyway.)*
 - **Reduced motion (M13):** the rAF counter is private and the wrapper non-writable; a non-finite or decreasing reading counts as a loop. UNTESTED: animation driven by timers or CSS that a page starts after the 700 ms window.
 - **Spacing (M15, M20):** `html` and `body` margins are screened; every `data-fannan-spacing-exception` needs a scoped handoff `spacingExceptions` entry naming the approver. UNTESTED: exceptions on pseudo-elements.
 - **Package (M12):** environment files (`.env*`), editor locks (`.#*`), credential folders (`.ssh`, `.gnupg`, `.aws`) and credential names (`credentials`, `secrets`, `service-account`, `token`, `.npmrc`, `.netrc`, `.pypirc`, `.git-credentials`) are refused with any suffix. Plural `tokens` stays allowed because design-token files are named `tokens.json`. UNTESTED: secrets inside ordinarily named files (names only; the secret grep is manual).
@@ -19,7 +32,7 @@ All browser checks below ran in Chrome 155 headless only.
 
 - **axe tags (C1):** `wcag21a` and `wcag22a` added; a test checks the set against the pinned axe-core 4.14.0 rule tags. axe's experimental A/AA rules (`css-orientation-lock`, `p-as-heading`, `table-fake-caption`, `td-has-header`) stay off and remain manual. UNTESTED: other axe versions.
 - **Accent (panel A):** bound to the approved `colors.accent`/`colors.primary` token. FAIL at handoff with the variable named; DEFERRED in wireframes. The area stays an approximate DOM proxy. UNTESTED: colour spaces beyond sRGB comparing equal after canvas normalisation.
-- **Glass (S2/C6, panel D):** computed on `html`, `body`, visible elements and rendered pseudo-elements, in open shadow roots and same-origin (srcdoc) frames, plus constructed stylesheets and raw-text scans of served CSS/HTML/SVG/JS, style attributes and `<style>`. Any raw `backdrop-filter` other than `none` fails, even when the rule never applies (fail closed). NOT COVERED: closed shadow roots (unreachable from script) and cross-origin frames (blocked by the checker; listed as `unscannedFrames`). `file://` frames are cross-origin in Chrome, so their glass is caught only by the served-file text scan. A `-webkit-` alias added by a script in a constructed sheet is caught only by that text scan (Chrome drops it when parsing). Styles injected later than the probes run are UNTESTED.
+- **Glass (S2/C6, panel D):** computed on `html`, `body`, visible elements and rendered pseudo-elements, in open shadow roots and same-origin (srcdoc) frames, plus constructed stylesheets and raw-text scans of served CSS/HTML/SVG/JS, style attributes and `<style>`. Any raw `backdrop-filter` other than `none` fails, even when the rule never applies (fail closed). NOT COVERED: closed shadow roots (unreachable from script) and cross-origin frames (blocked by the checker; listed as `unscannedFrames`). `file://` frames are cross-origin in Chrome, so their glass is caught only by the served-file text scan. A `-webkit-` alias added by a script in a constructed sheet is caught only by that text scan (Chrome drops it when parsing). Styles injected later than the probes run are UNTESTED. *(Superseded by R13 N21: frames are partially inspected and every frame fails the handoff.)*
 - **320 px reflow (S3, panel B):** candidates only, recorded and resolved by `reflowExceptions`; keyboard use means `tabindex` on the scroller or a focusable child. Chrome's automatic focusable scrollers are not counted. UNTESTED: `overflow: overlay`, scrollers in shadow roots, and whether a resolved candidate genuinely needs 2D layout (that is the reviewer's decision).
 - **Probe world and integrity (C3, panel C):** probes and axe run in a CDP isolated world (not a Playwright API). The page-world vs probe-world comparison, the native-function check (a heuristic: a page can hide a patch from `toString`) and the JavaScript-off pass run on the positional page only, not on every state. The JavaScript-off pass compares glass and the 320 px screen. Contrast is NOT cross-checked with JavaScript off, because axe does not complete with page scripts disabled in Chrome 155. Iframes get no isolated world of their own. Page scripts that change the DOM or CSS between the two world measurements could cause a false mismatch (UNTESTED).
 - **Package (C4, panel D):** explicit suffix allowlist plus denial of `.env*`, keys, certificates, credential dotfiles, OS junk, editor files and VCS files, both in package input and among changed paths. Checked with temporary trees. UNTESTED: secrets inside ordinarily named files (only names are screened; the separate secret grep is manual).
