release/skills/manage-design-system/SKILL.md
---
name: manage-design-system
description: Retrieve, create or update a Stitch design system for a project whose settings explicitly choose Stitch.
allowed-tools:
  - "stitch*:*"
  - Read
  - web_fetch
---

Use only after the current project's `design-tool:` selects Stitch, the pinned manifest is verified, and Step 5 desktop structure approval permits styling. Stitch is accessed through MCP with `STITCH_API_KEY` in the secret store. Read actual project/screen metadata and approved DESIGN.md, then show the proposed display name, color roles, fonts, roundness, affected screens and any cost. Wait for Fadel's written yes in Fannan's chat before upload, creation, application or any paid call. WCAG 2.2 AA is the floor. No shell uploader, direct key, CLI, repo edit or public link. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md).

Use `list_projects`, `list_screens`, `get_screen` and `list_design_systems` to ground the change. Have Fannan save and lint Google's DESIGN.md to zero errors in `/workspace/design-output/<project>/` after `$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh "/workspace/design-output/<project>/" "<project>"`. For an approved upload, use `upload_design_md` MCP, then `create_design_system_from_design_md` with its returned selected screen instance. For applying an existing system, get screen instances from `get_project` and pass only `{id, sourceScreen}` in `selectedScreenInstances`; the asset ID comes from `list_design_systems`. Read [Stitch MCP shapes](references/stitch-mcp-shapes.md) for exact fields. Record result and affected version. Respect the project's brief-derived type/palette; do not substitute vendor defaults.

## Gotchas

- `selectedScreenInstances` with position or dimension fields can fail; use only the two required fields.
- An upload is a system change and needs its own explicit approval even if the design was approved.
release/skills/shadcn/SKILL.md
---
name: shadcn
description: Read shadcn component guidance when the project's existing stack uses it; translate patterns into design specifications only.
allowed-tools: Read
---

Use only if the project's settings and read-only UI map show shadcn. Verify the pinned manifest through the session workflow. Read existing components and project tokens first; specify composition, semantic color roles, forms, focus, empty/loading/error and responsive behavior for the project's engineer. Follow [handoff contract](../../references/handoff-contract.md) and [design quality](../../references/design-quality.md). WCAG 2.2 AA and approved project rules outrank library defaults. Desktop stays grayscale through Step 5; no mobile before its approved step.

This is guidance only. Do not run shadcn CLI, `npx`, package installation, init/add commands, or edit repo files. If notes must be saved, route through a workflow that verifies the pinned manifest and runs `$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh "/workspace/design-output/<project>/" "<project>"` before writing there. Do not invent missing component APIs.

## Gotchas

- Library examples can suggest a component, but cannot choose the project's visual idea or copy.
- The engineer chooses actual code; Fannan records buildable specifications, not source patches.
release/skills/stitch-design-md/SKILL.md
---
name: stitch-design-md
description: Extract a Google-spec DESIGN.md proposal from an existing Stitch project selected in project settings.
allowed-tools:
  - "stitch*:*"
  - Read
  - web_fetch
---

Use only when `design-tool:` in project settings is Stitch and the session's pinned manifest check passed. Stitch access is MCP only; `STITCH_API_KEY` stays in the secret store. No shell upload script, CLI, direct API key, public upload or repo write. WCAG 2.2 AA is the floor. Before Fannan saves output, run `"$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh" "/workspace/design-output/<project>/" "<project>"` through the approved workflow. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md).

Discover the MCP namespace; identify the project from settings, list screens, fetch `get_screen`/`get_project` metadata and permitted HTML/screenshot assets. Extract actual color roles and hex values, typography, spacing/grid, geometry, depth, components and usage constraints. Trace the design system to the brief and approved stage. Return DESIGN.md text using Google's YAML token frontmatter and canonical sections; Fannan writes it in the output folder and runs `design.md lint` to zero errors. At Steps 4–5 keep only grayscale structure; no color/type application before Step 5 approval. Missing facts stay explicit; never infer a palette from a generic template.

## Gotchas

- A Stitch screen may contain default styling or AI copy. Treat it as evidence to inspect, not authority for project tokens or claims.
- This skill extracts text; design-system upload/change belongs to `manage-design-system` and needs Fadel's yes.
- Units (OPUS-R2-08): every spacing, rounded, breakpoint and component size token carries `px`, `rem` or `em` (component sizes: `rounded`, `padding*`, `margin*`, `gap`, `rowGap`, `columnGap`, `inset*`, `size`, `width`, `height`, `min/maxWidth`, `min/maxHeight`); only `0` may be bare. `designmd-to-sd` refuses a bare nonzero number with `units required`.
- A component's `typography` may reference a whole typography group, `"{typography.<name>}"`, as the design.md spec allows; Fannan expands it per property. Composite references anywhere else are refused.

